{
  "case_id": "2006-05-11304",
  "document_hash": "8bb86d93a27f0cf77bfdedc1b3c4960ad564d36f8ba433f423b99589a2c3303a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Jordan Steiker",
      "case_id": "2006-05-11304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8bb86d93a27f0cf77bfdedc1b3c4960ad564d36f8ba433f423b99589a2c3303a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8bb86d93a27f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case is here for the second time. In your summary of reversal, this Court held that Petitioner's mitigating evidence could not be given adequate consideration through the Texas special issues or the nullification instructions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-11304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8bb86d93a27f0cf77bfdedc1b3c4960ad564d36f8ba433f423b99589a2c3303a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8bb86d93a27f-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Did they find it could or did they find that it did? I thought our holding was that given the instructions, the jury would not necessarily take into account those mitigating factors, and I thought that what the Texas court held"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-11304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8bb86d93a27f0cf77bfdedc1b3c4960ad564d36f8ba433f423b99589a2c3303a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8bb86d93a27f-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you concede that harmless error analysis is ever appropriate, is ever open as an option following an, in effect, a finding of this kind of instructional error, Penry I instructional error? Do you concede that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jordan Steiker",
      "case_id": "2006-05-11304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8bb86d93a27f0cf77bfdedc1b3c4960ad564d36f8ba433f423b99589a2c3303a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8bb86d93a27f-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I believe that the CCA misunderstood the Federal law of the relationship between Penry I and Penry II. The failing in this case was a verdict form that made no mention of mitigating evidence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "STEIKER",
      "case_id": "2006-05-11304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8bb86d93a27f0cf77bfdedc1b3c4960ad564d36f8ba433f423b99589a2c3303a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8bb86d93a27f-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STEIKER: I think it would not be in the case of State habeas, for this reason. The vast overwhelming number of cases that proceed into State habeas are on their way when they're final into Federal habeas, and the State court was abandoning this argument for Federal habeas. That is, it was removing any procedural impediment to a merits review."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-11304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8bb86d93a27f0cf77bfdedc1b3c4960ad564d36f8ba433f423b99589a2c3303a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8bb86d93a27f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Especially in capital cases, courts don't like to say, oh, you know, yes, you may be innocent but there's this procedural objection. I think most courts --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-05-11304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8bb86d93a27f0cf77bfdedc1b3c4960ad564d36f8ba433f423b99589a2c3303a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8bb86d93a27f-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: But even if it is, logically anterior to consideration of that procedural impediment is a particular ruling on the merits and the State court didn't make that merits. They thought there was no error."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "CRUZ",
      "case_id": "2006-05-11304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8bb86d93a27f0cf77bfdedc1b3c4960ad564d36f8ba433f423b99589a2c3303a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8bb86d93a27f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CRUZ: I do not disagree with you that if the State court had concluded for Petitioner on a State ground TO begin with and after being reversed revisited that conclusion --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-11304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8bb86d93a27f0cf77bfdedc1b3c4960ad564d36f8ba433f423b99589a2c3303a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8bb86d93a27f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What is the argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-05-11304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8bb86d93a27f0cf77bfdedc1b3c4960ad564d36f8ba433f423b99589a2c3303a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8bb86d93a27f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Really?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-11304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8bb86d93a27f0cf77bfdedc1b3c4960ad564d36f8ba433f423b99589a2c3303a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8bb86d93a27f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What instruction? I haven't seen one."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-11304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8bb86d93a27f0cf77bfdedc1b3c4960ad564d36f8ba433f423b99589a2c3303a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8bb86d93a27f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: When you say 90 percent, you're talking about argument time, aren't you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "California, et al.",
      "case_id": "2006-05-11304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8bb86d93a27f0cf77bfdedc1b3c4960ad564d36f8ba433f423b99589a2c3303a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8bb86d93a27f-0002-0008",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I represent California and 20 other states who are concerned about the implications of Petitioner's arguments for their ability to apply their own varied harmless error standards in their own State habeas proceedings, and thereby to strike what they believe to be the right balance between the two competing concerns that this Court identified in Calderon."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-11304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8bb86d93a27f0cf77bfdedc1b3c4960ad564d36f8ba433f423b99589a2c3303a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8bb86d93a27f-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Are you talking about both collateral review and direct review, or just collateral review?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-11304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8bb86d93a27f0cf77bfdedc1b3c4960ad564d36f8ba433f423b99589a2c3303a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8bb86d93a27f-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: In, in this case suppose the following circumstance. Suppose a Federal court has decided in the case of this defendant --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-11304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8bb86d93a27f0cf77bfdedc1b3c4960ad564d36f8ba433f423b99589a2c3303a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8bb86d93a27f-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Have you ever seen it in a State? Have you ever seen a State which gets a case back from --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-11304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8bb86d93a27f0cf77bfdedc1b3c4960ad564d36f8ba433f423b99589a2c3303a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8bb86d93a27f-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Is there some reason, Mr. Schaerr, why that would be more egregious when the Federal constitutional question has been answered by a Federal district court than it is when the Federal constitutional question has been answered by the State supreme court?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-05-11304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8bb86d93a27f0cf77bfdedc1b3c4960ad564d36f8ba433f423b99589a2c3303a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8bb86d93a27f-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: What about General, Mr. Cruz's comments that this was a minor point in counsel's summation before the jury?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2006-05-11304",
      "confidence": 0.0,
